## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | lib/src/compaction/record_tag.dart | 🚨 blocking ci red — the crap gate fails on recordtagechostreamfilter push crap 18 00 vs threshold 12 00 the crap duplication check fails on this commit fa2e11ca and the offender is new code introduced by this pr 18 00 100 0 n a 18 recordtagechostreamfilter push lib src compaction record tag dart 130 max crap 18 00 — fail threshold 12 00 the project s crap ratchet is pinned at 12 0 crap4dart yaml 51 and only ever moves down a new symbol scoring 18 breaks the gate ci classification json classifies the failure as owned the complexity comes from the single push method concentrating the whole state machine one switch with 10 guarded cases over 4 states plus the per byte loop and buffer management split the state handling out of push so each method stays simple — e g extract the linestart alias spaces arms into small private helpers classifylinestart int ch classifyalias int ch … and keep push as the loop dispatch that drops each function s complexity below the ratchet without changing the already well tested semantics |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/compaction/record_tag.dart | ⚠️ important the stream filter diverges from the gh 2412 persist seam for leading aliases without a trailing space — the tag still reaches the user live the pr description says the undecided tail flush follows the gh 2412 m d regex semantics but the gh 2412 echo contract has two rules and this filter implements only one 1 striprecordtags — per line m d record tag dart 43 — implemented ✅ tests pin the parity 2 the leading alias rule — leadingalias regexp r m d s trimleft on the first text block record tag echo dart 16 24 applied at the finalize seam the pr itself names as the boundary agent dart 1102 withoutrecordtagecho its doc is explicit a reply whose first text block opens with an alias that ends there — m3208 is a reply that is only its tag flush line 167 releases an undecided m d tail verbatim so the streaming faces paint what the seam strips at finalize reproduced against the real classes each line filter output vs striprecordtagecho result tag only reply live m3208 seam final alias newline live m3208 nреальный ответ seam final реальный ответ consequences per face the app s live bubble shows m3208 for the whole turn and it vanishes at finalize a flash of exactly what gh 2472 bans the cli s raw face keeps it painted and the buffered ansi plain faces render it permanently into assistanttext nothing re cleans that buffer — it disagrees with the tui replay of the same stored message which strips the tag only shape is not hypothetical the tagging machinery itself produces tag only text blocks for pure tool call carriers record tag dart 384 fix teach the filter the leading alias rule — the first line start candidate of a message not just of a line that reaches end of message newline without a trailing space must be classified against m d s instead of flushed verbatim every subsequent line keeps the current m d semantics please also add the missing parity test against striprecordtagecho the current suite pins parity with striprecordtags only which is why this slipped through if the owner confirms tag only carrier replies occur in production streams this is upgradeable to 🚨 blocking — today i tier it ⚠️ because the ticket s stated ac shape m1482 with the trailing space is handled correctly everywhere |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

